cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the archived release below.
title: >-
  evidence-closed-loop: reference implementation for a unified dynamical
  theory of catatonia recovery from an evidence-coupled bistable cascade
abstract: >-
  Numerical corroboration for the theorems of the accompanying theory paper,
  and regeneration of the paper's display items. The proofs are in the
  manuscript; this software checks the quantitative statements and reproduces
  Table 1, Figure 1, Table 2 and Table 3 in the order in which they appear
  there, both as printed tables and as drawn PNG files.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Saito
    given-names: Hiroki
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4964-8559"
    affiliation: >-
      Onda-Daini Hospital, Chiba, Japan; Department of Neuropsychiatry,
      Nippon Medical School, Tokyo, Japan
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/entrance4-png/evidence-closed-loop"
keywords:
  - catatonia
  - computational psychiatry
  - dynamical systems
  - bistability
  - Allee threshold
  - Fisher information
  - asymptotically autonomous systems
  - reproducibility
